#X obj 60 1076 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlets\ and\ outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1104 Inlet: messages (see Messages) \; Outlet 0 \, 1: signal left / right (~55.9 kHz resampled) \; Outlet 2: info \, fm \, voice \, voicedata \, channel \, status \, \;   display <title> <value> (Launchkey) \, lcd (splash \, once), f 64;
#X obj 60 1196 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1224 note <p> <v> [ch] \, cc <n> <v> [ch] \, pgm <n> [ch] \, \;   bend <-8192..8191> [ch] \; <float> / list \, midi <bytes>: raw MIDI bytes ([midiin]) \, \;   SysEx parameter changes and voice dumps included \; bank <I|A|B|C|D> <1-32>: select a voice \; fm <control> <0-127> \, fminfo <control>: FM view \; <name> <value>: a voice parameter \, TX81Z data value \, \;   e.g. alg 4 \, out1 99 (all names: Voice parameters) \; n <name> <0-127>: the same from a pot / CC position \; ninfo <name>: outlet 2 gets info <name> <0-127> <value> \, \;   every change is reported this way by itself \; vced <p> <d> \, aced <p> <d>: raw parameter change \; dumpreq: report every value again (info \, fm \, channel) \; getvoice: outlet 2 gets voicedata <name> <93 VCED> \;   <23 ACED> \, voicedata ...: load that voice \; random <kind> [seed]: a new voice \, \;   kind: pluck bass lead brass pad strings total \; presetstep [n] \, userstep [n]: ROM preset A01-D32 / user \;   slot n after the one played last (the Launchkey pads) \; init: the TX81Z Init Voice \; user <0-63>: recall a slot of the user bank \; store [0-63] \, save: the voice into a slot (save: the last \;   one) \, writes txuser-bank.syx (two TX81Z voice dumps) \; userread [file] \, userwrite [file]: the user bank \; channel <0-16>: receive channel \, 0 = omni \; tune <0-127>: master tune (64 = centre) \; rom <file> \, nvram <file>: load (the nvram is only read) \; factoryinit: all notes off \, voice A01 \; gain <f>: output gain (default 1), f 64;
#X obj 60 1716 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Editors\ (txfm\ and\ txedit) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1744 [txfm \$0-tx81zn] above: the FM editor \, 7 rows of 8 controls = the Launchkey pages of txfmcc. On top: voice name \, bank I A B C D and patch \, the algorithm with its roles \, random voices. [txedit \$0-tx81zn]: all 100 voice parameters in rows of 8 \, voice name \, program change \, MIDI channel \, user bank (txuser-bank.syx: 64 voices as two TX81Z voice bulk dumps \, kept by the object). Both work on the same bus and stay in sync \, click to open them. \; In your own patch: [r tx1] -> [tx81zn~ <rom> <nvram>] -> outlet 2 -> [s tx1-out] \, [txfm tx1] \, [txedit tx1] \, [r tx1-out] -> [txfmcc 0] -> [s tx1]., f 64;
#X obj 60 1948 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty FM\ view 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1976 The FM view gives the four operators roles from the algorithm: C = the carriers (what you hear) \, A = the modulator of the main carrier OP1 \, B = the other modulators. A control of a role changes all of its operators and shows the value of the first one. In the end everything is an ordinary TX81Z voice parameter: the voice stays a TX81Z voice (txedit shows every single value). \; Algorithms (> = modulates) and roles: 1 4>3>2>1 C:1 A:2 B:3+4 \, 2 (4+3)>2>1 C:1 A:2 B:3+4 \, 3 (4+(3>2))>1 C:1 A:2 B:3+4 \, 4 ((4>3)+2)>1 C:1 A:2 B:3+4 \, 5 (4>3)+(2>1) C:1+3 A:2 B:4 \, 6 4>(3+2+1) C:1+2+3 A:4 B:- \, 7 (4>3)+2+1 C:1+2+3 A:4 B:- \, 8 4+3+2+1 C:1+2+3+4 A:- B:-. \; Ratio shows the real frequency ratio of coarse and fine. Mix: left the main carrier OP1 \, right the other carriers (the louder side keeps its level). Detune spreads all operators around the centre. ENV C is the amplitude \, ENV A and ENV B are the brightness. Changing the algorithm keeps the operator settings: an operator that becomes a carrier sounds with its output level. \; page 1 PERFORM \, CC 20-27: moda mod A \, fdbk feedback \, atkc attack \, relc release \, lpmd pitch depth \, dtun detune \, mix mix \, vol volume \; page 2 SYN 1 \, CC 28-31 33-36: algo algorithm \, ratc ratio C \, rata ratio A \, ratb ratio B \, modb mod B \, lvlc level C \; page 3 SYN 2 \, CC 37 39-45: wavc wave C \, wava wave A \, wavb wave B \, finc fine C \, fina fine A \, finb fine B \; page 4 ENV C \, CC 46-53: decc decay \, susc sustain \, d2rc fade \, velc velocity \, lscc key level \, rscc key rate \; page 5 ENV A \, CC 54-61: atka attack \, deca decay \, susa sustain \, d2ra fade \, rela release \, vela velocity \, lsca key level \, rsca key rate \; page 6 ENV B \, CC 62-63 70-75: atkb attack \, decb decay \, susb sustain \, d2rb fade \, relb release \, velb velocity \, lscb key level \, rscb key rate \; page 7 LFO \, CC 76-83: lspd speed \, lwav wave \, ldly delay \, lamd amp depth \, lpms pitch sens \, lams amp sens \, lsyn key sync \; page 8 VOICE \, CC 85-87 89-93: poly poly/mono \, pbr bend range \, pmod porta mode \, port porta time \, trps transpose \, amec LFO amp C \, amea LFO amp A \, ameb LFO amp B, f 64;
#X obj 60 2628 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MIDI\ CC:\ controller\ layer\ (txfmcc) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2656 [txfmcc 0] above is the controller layer for the FM view: Launchkey pages 1-7 = the 7 rows of the editor txfm (CC 20-83) \, transpose is on CC 80 (page 7 VOICE \, encoder 5). It follows the receive channel tx81zn~ reports (0 = omni = all channels). \; Changes from elsewhere (voice change \, editor \, messages) go back to the controller as CC \, one every 2 ms. Pickup: after such a change an encoder acts only when it reaches the value or crosses it (pickup 0 turns that off). CC 3 or sync sends all values to the controller. \; For the single parameters use [txcc] of tx81z~ instead (CC pages 20-119 \, n <name> <0-127>): tx81zn~ takes the same messages., f 64;
#X obj 60 2892 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Launchkey 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2920 Launchkey: the Novation Launchkey Mini MK4 with the custom firmware maltepeter2000/launchkey_firmware \, set up the same for every instrument of bela-workstation (launchkey/README.md there). \; txfmcc 1: the controller layer. Encoders in mode Custom 1 send CC pages from 20 in rows of 8 on the keys channel \, every change made elsewhere goes back to them on the send channel (txchannel of tx81zn~) \, CC 3 asks for all values. \; txpads 10: the pads in Drum mode (notes 36-51 on channel 10 \, the Drums Channel): top row 36 factory + \, 37 user + \, 38 init (press twice within a second) \, 39-43 own \, bottom row 44 factory - \, 45 user - \, 46 save \, 47-51 own. Own pads of tx81zn~: 39-43 random pluck \, bass \, lead \, brass \, pad \, 47 random strings \, 48 random total. \; Pad colours \, sent by txpads itself with noteout on channel 10 (velocity = colour + 32 x mode): factory blue \, user green \, init orange (flashing while the second press is awaited) \, save red (white for a moment when pressed) \, own pads purple \, free pads off. They go out at load \, on leds \, and when the Launchkey asks for them (CC 3 = 127 on channel 10 \, sent when Drum mode is selected). \; lkdisplay: the display lines (display <title> <value>: the control you turn \, Preset \, User \, Init or Stored with the patch name) as SysEx for the Launchkey's display -> midiout. \; channel 1 at load (below): the pads on channel 10 must not play notes \, so the help patch sets the receive channel to 1., f 64;
#X obj 82 3364 txpads 10;
