#X obj 60 3503 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ of\ the\ FM\ view\ (0-127) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3531 algo: algorithm 1-8 \, it sets the roles C / A / B. \; ratc: frequency ratio of the carriers C. \; rata: frequency ratio of modulator A. \; ratb: frequency ratio of the modulators B. \; moda: output level of A = brightness. \; modb: output level of B. \; fdbk: feedback of operator 4 \, 0-7. \; mix: carriers against each other (only with several: algorithms 5-8)., f 64;
#X obj 60 3703 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Voice\ parameters 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3731 Voice (data values as stored in the TX81Z): \; alg 0-7: algorithm (1-8 on the TX81Z) \; fb 0-7: feedback of operator 4 \; lfs 0-99: lfo speed \; lfd 0-99: lfo delay \; pmd 0-99: pitch modulation depth \; amd 0-99: amplitude modulation depth \; sync 0-1: LFO key sync \; lfw 0-3: LFO wave: saw square triangle S/H \; pms 0-7: pitch modulation sensitivity \; ams 0-3: amplitude modulation sensitivity \; trps 0-48: transpose (24 = middle C) \; poly 0-1: poly / mono \; pbr 0-12: pitch bend range in semitones \; pmod 0-1: portamento mode (full time) \; port 0-99: portamento time \; fcv 0-99: foot controller volume \; sus 0-1: sustain on / off \; pon 0-1: portamento on / off \; chor 0-1: chorus (set 0) \; mwp 0-99: mod wheel pitch \; mwa 0-99: mod wheel amplitude \; bcp 0-99: breath control pitch \; bca 0-99: breath control amplitude \; bcpb 0-99: breath control pitch bias (50 = centre) \; bceb 0-99: breath control EG bias \; rev 0-7: reverb rate (0 = off \, 7 = fast) \; fcp 0-99: foot controller pitch \; fca 0-99: foot controller amplitude \;   \; Operators: name + operator number 1-4 \, e.g. ar1 \, osw4: \; ar1-ar4 0-31: attack rate \; d1r1-d1r4 0-31: decay 1 rate \; d2r1-d2r4 0-31: decay 2 rate \; rr1-rr4 0-15: release rate \; d1l1-d1l4 0-15: decay 1 level \; ls1-ls4 0-99: level scaling \; rs1-rs4 0-3: rate scaling \; ebs1-ebs4 0-7: EG bias sensitivity \; ame1-ame4 0-1: amplitude modulation on / off \; kvs1-kvs4 0-7: key velocity sensitivity \; out1-out4 0-99: output level \; crs1-crs4 0-63: frequency coarse \; det1-det4 0-6: detune (3 = centre) \; fix1-fix4 0-1: fixed frequency (0 ratio \, 1 fixed) \; fixr1-fixr4 0-7: fixed range 250 Hz ... 32 kHz \; fin1-fin4 0-15: frequency fine \; osw1-osw4 0-7: waveform W1-W8 (0-7) \; sh1-sh4 0-3: EG shift: 0 96 dB \, 1 48 \, 2 24 \, 3 12, f 64;
#X obj 60 4543 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty How\ it\ works 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4571 The voice \, note \, modulation and controller routines of the TX81Z firmware v1.6 are rebuilt in C++ and drive the YM2414 directly \, with the same register values as the firmware (tested against the firmware running in tx81z~). A YM2414 core derived from ymfm \, bit-identical to it \, renders the sound. About a third to a sixth of the CPU of tx81z~ \, and parameter changes take effect at once (no SysEx round trip). \; Single mode only: no performance mode \, no micro tuning \, no front panel. The display shows the splash screen once (lcd)\; the voice name comes as voice <name>., f 64;
#X obj 60 4759 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty ROM\ and\ battery\ RAM 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4787 Arguments: [tx81zn~ <firmware> <battery RAM file>] \, paths relative to the patch. The firmware (64 KB \, e.g. tx81z-v1.6.bin from the MAME set tx81z) is not included: tx81zn~ reads its tables and the preset banks A-D from it. The battery RAM file of tx81z~ is optional and only read: bank I \, master tune and receive channel. tx81zn~ never writes it \, so a channel set here lasts until the patch closes\; without the file tx81zn~ receives omni., f 64;
#X obj 60 4943 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Voices 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4971 bank <I|A|B|C|D> <1-32> selects any voice \, bank D included. Program change 0-127 selects I01-I32 and A01-C32 as on the TX81Z (I 0-31 \, A 32-63 \, B 64-95 \, C 96-127). Bank I comes from the battery RAM file\; without it bank I is empty. random <kind> [seed] makes a new voice (the same generator as tx81z~)., f 64;
